      "notes": "vLLM V2 on dual RTX 5060 Ti 16GB (Unraid 7, 6.18.38). MTP speculative decoding: num_speculative_tokens=3, TP=2, NVFP4 quant, max-model-len 131072, KV-cache nvfp4 4.5GB budget, prefix-caching + chunked-prefill enabled, cudagraph_capture_sizes [1,2,4,8,16]. This is the warm-cache representative run (4 consecutive back-to-back benchmark iterations, prefix cache hot): 63.2-63.7 tok/s decode, ~186-195 ms TTFT. MTP draft acceptance during this window: avg 54.8% (41.4-71.1%, p50 52.6%, 18 samples) — well above the ~30% breakeven for 3 draft tokens, i.e. MTP spec-decode is net-positive here. For contrast, a cold-cache benchmark window earlier in the session measured 38.2 tok/s at ~35% acceptance; full-lifetime real-world Hermes traffic averages ~50.6% token-weighted acceptance (2.69M samples, per-position pos1=0.647 pos2=0.495 pos3=0.393). Engine: vLLM, quant NVFP4.",
